   "source": [
    "# 🌾 Rice Leaf Disease Detection — a CNN Built From Scratch \n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook classifies a photo of a rice leaf as **Bacterial leaf blight**, **Brown spot** or **Leaf smut** using a convolutional neural network in which **every layer, every gradient and the optimiser are written by hand in NumPy**.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### Contents\n",
    "1. Setup & configuration\n",
    "2. Dataset audit\n",
    "3. Loading & stratified train / validation / test split\n",
    "4. Data augmentation\n",
    "5. The CNN engine, layer by layer, with the maths\n",
    "6. Verifying every gradient numerically\n",
    "7. Model architecture\n",
    "8. Training\n",
    "9. Evaluation on test set\n",
    "10. 5-fold cross-validation\n",
    "11. Saving the model & predicting a single image\n",
    "12. Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data:** [UCI Rice Leaf Diseases](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/486/rice+leaf+diseases) (120 JPGs, 40 per class, CC BY 4.0). Put it in a folder `mydata/` with one sub-folder per class:\n",
    "```\n",
    "mydata/Bacterial leaf blight/   mydata/Brown spot/   mydata/Leaf smut/\n",
    "```\n",
    "**Requirements:** `numpy`, `pillow`, `matplotlib`. "
   ]
  },
