    "## 2. Dataset audit\n",
    "\n",
    "Before modelling, look at the data. Two findings drive the design:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Shape.** Most images are 3081 × 897 pixels: long horizontal leaves. Squashing them into a 64 × 64 square, as v1 did, compresses the length ~3.4× more than the width and destroys lesion detail. We therefore use **80 × 256** inputs.\n",
    "* **Resolution is correlated with the label.** All *Bacterial leaf blight* images are 3081 × 897, while the other classes mix sizes from several sources. Every image is resized to the same input size, but the model could still pick up resampling or JPEG artefacts. Keep this in mind when reading the (perfect) Bacterial-leaf-blight scores."
   ]
  },
