    "## 3. Loading & stratified train / validation / test split\n",
    "\n",
    "* Each image is converted to RGB, rotated to landscape if needed, and resized to 80 × 256 with bicubic resampling.\n",
    "* The split is **stratified** (identical class proportions in every subset) and has **three** parts:\n",
    "  * **train** fits the weights;\n",
    "  * **validation** chooses the best epoch (early stopping);\n",
    "  * **test** is used **exactly once**, at the very end.\n",
    "\n",
    "  v1 picked its best epoch on the validation set and then reported that same set as its result. That is selection bias and makes the score optimistic.\n",
    "* Pixels are standardised per channel, using mean and standard deviation computed **on the training images only**, so nothing leaks from validation or test:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\hat{x}_{c,i,j} = \\frac{x_{c,i,j} - \\mu_c}{\\sigma_c},\\qquad \\mu_c = \\frac{1}{N_{\\text{train}}HW}\\sum_{n,i,j}x^{(n)}_{c,i,j}.$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "8d9c9aaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded images: (119, 80, 256, 3) in 2.1s\n",
      "train        83 images  per class: [28, 28, 27]\n",
      "validation   18 images  per class: [6, 6, 6]\n",
      "test         18 images  per class: [6, 6, 6]\n"
     ]
    }
