    "## 5. The CNN engine, layer by layer\n",
    "\n",
    "Tensors use the layout $(N, C, H, W)$: batch, channels, height, width.\n",
    "\n",
    "Training minimises a scalar loss $L(\\theta)$ by gradient descent. Each layer therefore implements two maps:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **forward:** $Y = f(X;\\theta)$, caching whatever the backward pass will need;\n",
    "* **backward:** given the upstream gradient $\\delta Y=\\partial L/\\partial Y$, return $\\delta X$ for the previous layer and store $\\delta\\theta$ for the optimiser.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both come from the chain rule, applied one layer at a time:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial X}=\\Big(\\frac{\\partial Y}{\\partial X}\\Big)^{\\!\\top}\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial Y},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\theta}=\\Big(\\frac{\\partial Y}{\\partial \\theta}\\Big)^{\\!\\top}\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial Y}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Convolution as matrix multiplication: im2col\n",
    "\n",
    "A convolution layer slides $F$ learned filters $W\\in\\mathbb{R}^{F\\times C\\times k\\times k}$ over the input. Deep-learning \"convolution\" is strictly **cross-correlation** (the kernel is not flipped):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$Y_{n,f,i,j}=b_f+\\sum_{c=1}^{C}\\sum_{u=0}^{k-1}\\sum_{v=0}^{k-1}W_{f,c,u,v}\\,X^{\\text{pad}}_{n,c,\\,is+u,\\,js+v},\\qquad H_{\\text{out}}=\\Big\\lfloor\\frac{H+2p-k}{s}\\Big\\rfloor+1.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Six nested Python loops would be far too slow. **im2col** instead unrolls every $k\\times k\\times C$ receptive field into one row of a matrix $X_{\\text{col}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{(NH_{\\text{out}}W_{\\text{out}})\\times(Ck^2)}$. The whole convolution then becomes **one matrix multiply**, which NumPy runs with optimised BLAS:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$Y_{\\text{mat}} = X_{\\text{col}}\\,W_{\\text{mat}}^{\\top}+\\mathbf 1 b^{\\top},\\qquad W_{\\text{mat}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{F\\times Ck^2}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "`im2col` builds a zero-copy strided **view** with shape $(N,H_{\\text{out}},W_{\\text{out}},C,k,k)$. **col2im** is its adjoint (transpose): it scatter-*adds* rows back to pixel positions. The adding matters because overlapping windows share input pixels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "4791f066",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def conv_output_size(n, k, stride, pad):\n",
    "    return (n + 2 * pad - k) // stride + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def im2col(x, kh, kw, stride=1, pad=0):\n",
    "    n, c, h, w = x.shape\n",
    "    if pad:\n",
    "        x = np.pad(x, ((0, 0), (0, 0), (pad, pad), (pad, pad)))\n",
    "    ho, wo = conv_output_size(h, kh, stride, pad), conv_output_size(w, kw, stride, pad)\n",
    "    s_n, s_c, s_h, s_w = x.strides\n",
    "    windows = as_strided(x, shape=(n, ho, wo, c, kh, kw),\n",
    "                         strides=(s_n, s_h * stride, s_w * stride, s_c, s_h, s_w), writeable=False)\n",
    "    return windows.reshape(n * ho * wo, c * kh * kw), ho, wo\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def col2im(cols, x_shape, kh, kw, stride=1, pad=0):\n",
    "    n, c, h, w = x_shape\n",
    "    ho, wo = conv_output_size(h, kh, stride, pad), conv_output_size(w, kw, stride, pad)\n",
    "    cols6 = cols.reshape(n, ho, wo, c, kh, kw)\n",
    "    dx = np.zeros((n, c, h + 2 * pad, w + 2 * pad), dtype=cols.dtype)\n",
    "    for i in range(kh):\n",
    "        for j in range(kw):\n",
    "            dx[:, :, i:i + stride * ho:stride, j:j + stride * wo:stride] += cols6[:, :, :, :, i, j].transpose(0, 3, 1, 2)\n",
    "    return dx[:, :, pad:-pad, pad:-pad] if pad else dx\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def log_softmax(z):\n",
    "    z = z - z.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n",
    "    return z - np.log(np.exp(z).sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def softmax(z):\n",
    "    return np.exp(log_softmax(z))"
   ]
  },
  {
