    "### 5.3 Batch normalisation\n",
    "\n",
    "Each channel is normalised over the $m=NHW$ values it takes in the batch, then rescaled by a learned $\\gamma$ and shifted by a learned $\\beta$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mu=\\tfrac1m\\textstyle\\sum x,\\qquad \\sigma^2=\\tfrac1m\\sum(x-\\mu)^2,\\qquad \\hat x=\\dfrac{x-\\mu}{\\sqrt{\\sigma^2+\\varepsilon}},\\qquad y=\\gamma\\hat x+\\beta.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "BatchNorm keeps activations in a stable range, which tolerates larger learning rates. A convolution bias right before BN would be cancelled by the mean subtraction, so those convolutions use `bias=False`.\n",
    "\n",
    "At **inference** there is no batch to normalise over, so running averages collected during training are used instead ($\\mu_{\\text{run}}\\leftarrow0.9\\,\\mu_{\\text{run}}+0.1\\,\\mu$, with the unbiased variance).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Backward.** $\\hat x$ depends on the whole batch through $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$, so the gradient has three terms. With $g=\\gamma\\,\\delta y$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial\\beta}=\\sum\\delta y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial\\gamma}=\\sum\\delta y\\,\\hat x,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial x}=\\frac{1}{m\\sqrt{\\sigma^2+\\varepsilon}}\\Big(m\\,g-\\sum g-\\hat x\\sum g\\,\\hat x\\Big).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The two subtracted terms remove the parts of the gradient that would only shift the batch mean or rescale its variance, since normalisation undoes both anyway."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "69afa79a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class BatchNorm2D(Layer):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, c, momentum=0.9, eps=1e-5):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.c, self.momentum, self.eps = c, momentum, eps\n",
    "        self.params[\"gamma\"] = np.ones(c, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        self.params[\"beta\"] = np.zeros(c, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        self.running_mean = np.zeros(c, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "        self.running_var = np.ones(c, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def buffers(self): return {\"running_mean\": self.running_mean, \"running_var\": self.running_var}\n",
    "    def no_decay(self): return {\"gamma\", \"beta\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def _bc(v): return v[None, :, None, None]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        if self.training:\n",
    "            mu, var = x.mean(axis=(0, 2, 3)), x.var(axis=(0, 2, 3))\n",
    "            m = x.shape[0] * x.shape[2] * x.shape[3]\n",
    "            self.running_mean[...] = self.momentum * self.running_mean + (1 - self.momentum) * mu\n",
    "            self.running_var[...] = self.momentum * self.running_var + (1 - self.momentum) * var * m / max(m - 1, 1)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            mu, var = self.running_mean, self.running_var\n",
    "        inv_std = 1.0 / np.sqrt(var + self.eps)\n",
    "        x_hat = (x - self._bc(mu)) * self._bc(inv_std)\n",
    "        if self.training:\n",
    "            self._cache = (x_hat, inv_std)\n",
    "        return self._bc(self.params[\"gamma\"]) * x_hat + self._bc(self.params[\"beta\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "    def backward(self, dout):\n",
    "        x_hat, inv_std = self._cache\n",
    "        ax = (0, 2, 3)\n",
    "        m = dout.shape[0] * dout.shape[2] * dout.shape[3]\n",
    "        self.grads[\"beta\"] = dout.sum(axis=ax)\n",
    "        self.grads[\"gamma\"] = (dout * x_hat).sum(axis=ax)\n",
    "        g = dout * self._bc(self.params[\"gamma\"])\n",
    "        self._cache = None\n",
    "        return self._bc(inv_std / m) * (m * g - self._bc(g.sum(axis=ax)) - x_hat * self._bc((g * x_hat).sum(axis=ax)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __repr__(self): return f\"BatchNorm2D({self.c})\""
   ]
  },
