    "### 5.5 Softmax + cross-entropy with label smoothing\n",
    "\n",
    "Softmax turns logits into probabilities. It is computed stably by subtracting $\\max_k z_k$ first, which leaves the result unchanged but prevents `exp` from overflowing:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$p_k=\\frac{e^{z_k}}{\\sum_j e^{z_j}}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Label smoothing** ($\\varepsilon=0.1$) replaces the one-hot target with $t_k=(1-\\varepsilon)\\,\\mathbb 1[k=y]+\\varepsilon/K$, so the correct class gets 0.933 rather than 1. The loss is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$L=-\\frac1N\\sum_{n}\\sum_{k}t_{n,k}\\log p_{n,k}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Its gradient with respect to the logits is remarkably simple:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial z_{n,k}}=\\frac{1}{N}\\big(p_{n,k}-t_{n,k}\\big).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "*Derivation:* $\\partial\\log p_k/\\partial z_j=\\mathbb 1[k=j]-p_j$, so $\\partial L_n/\\partial z_j=-\\sum_k t_k(\\mathbb 1[k=j]-p_j)=p_j-t_j$, because the targets sum to 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "Without smoothing, the loss only reaches zero as the logit gap goes to infinity, which rewards over-confidence. That matters on a dataset this small."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "fd472248",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def softmax_cross_entropy(logits, y, label_smoothing=0.0):\n",
    "    n, k = logits.shape\n",
    "    logp = log_softmax(logits.astype(np.float64))\n",
    "    target = np.full((n, k), label_smoothing / k)\n",
    "    target[np.arange(n), y] += 1.0 - label_smoothing\n",
    "    loss = float(-(target * logp).sum(axis=1).mean())\n",
    "    return loss, ((np.exp(logp) - target) / n).astype(logits.dtype)"
   ]
  },
