    "### 5.6 Optimiser (AdamW), learning-rate schedule, gradient clipping\n",
    "\n",
    "**AdamW.** For each parameter $\\theta$ with gradient $g_t$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$m_t=\\beta_1m_{t-1}+(1-\\beta_1)g_t,\\qquad v_t=\\beta_2v_{t-1}+(1-\\beta_2)g_t^2,\\qquad \\hat m_t=\\frac{m_t}{1-\\beta_1^t},\\quad \\hat v_t=\\frac{v_t}{1-\\beta_2^t},$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\theta_t=\\theta_{t-1}-\\eta_t\\Big(\\frac{\\hat m_t}{\\sqrt{\\hat v_t}+\\epsilon}+\\lambda\\,\\theta_{t-1}\\Big).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "* The momentum $m$ smooths noisy mini-batch gradients; $v$ gives each parameter its own step size.\n",
    "* Both start at zero, so early estimates are biased towards zero; dividing by $1-\\beta^t$ corrects this.\n",
    "* Weight decay is **decoupled** (applied outside the adaptive fraction), so every weight shrinks at the same relative rate. Biases and BatchNorm $\\gamma,\\beta$ are exempt.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Schedule.** A linear warm-up over the first $T_w$ steps (3 epochs), then cosine annealing:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\eta_t=\\eta_{\\min}+\\tfrac12(\\eta_{\\max}-\\eta_{\\min})\\Big(1+\\cos\\big(\\pi\\tfrac{t-T_w}{T-T_w}\\big)\\Big).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Warm-up avoids large, badly directed steps while Adam's moments and BatchNorm's statistics are still unreliable.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Gradient clipping.** If $\\lVert g\\rVert_2>\\tau=5$, all gradients are rescaled by $\\tau/\\lVert g\\rVert_2$. The direction is kept; only exploding steps are capped."
   ]
  },
