    "## 6. Verifying every gradient \n",
    "\n",
    "A hand-written backward pass is easy to get subtly wrong, and a wrong gradient still \"trains\", just badly. So every analytic gradient is compared with a **central finite difference**, computed in float64:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial\\theta_i}\\approx\\frac{L(\\theta+h e_i)-L(\\theta-h e_i)}{2h},\\qquad h=10^{-5},\\qquad \\text{rel. error}=\\frac{|g_{\\text{analytic}}-g_{\\text{numeric}}|}{|g_{\\text{analytic}}|+|g_{\\text{numeric}}|}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For each layer we use $L=\\sum Y\\odot R$ with a fixed random $R$, so that $\\delta Y=R$. Correct gradients give relative errors around $10^{-8}$ or smaller; we require below $10^{-6}$."
   ]
  },
