    "The validation score is higher than the test score because the validation set was used to *choose* the epoch, and whatever set you choose on looks better than it really is. That is exactly why the test set is kept separate.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run-to-run variation.** An earlier run of the same model (as a Python package, with a few arithmetic steps written in a different order) scored 15/18 = 83.3 % on this same test set. Float32 rounding differs slightly, and over 57 epochs the training drifts onto a different path. One image more or less correct moves accuracy by 5.6 points, which is why the cross-validation below is the number to trust.\n",
    "\n",
    "The errors are confusions between **Brown spot** and **Leaf smut**, which both show small dark lesions. Bacterial leaf blight's long straw-coloured streaks are easy to separate (but see the resolution caveat in section 2)."
   ]
