    "## 10. 5-fold cross-validation\n",
    "\n",
    "A single split of 120 images is noisy: which 18 images land in the test set changes the result a lot. **Stratified 5-fold cross-validation** makes every image a test image exactly once. In each fold, 24 images test and the remaining 96 are split into 78 train and 18 validation (for early stopping). We report the fold mean ± standard deviation and the pooled out-of-fold confusion matrix."
   ]
