    "## 11. Saving the model & predicting a single image\n",
    "\n",
    "The checkpoint is a single `.npz` file containing the weights **and** everything needed to use them: class names, input size, and normalisation statistics. The prediction function therefore never relies on global variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "`predict_image` returns the label, the confidence and all class probabilities, plus an `uncertain` flag when the top probability is below a threshold. The model only knows these three diseases, so a healthy leaf would still be forced into one of them; the flag is a cue for human review."
   ]
  },
